-- A per-row fold over a fiber column, where two of the four fibers are empty. +/ declares the identity 0 and answers every row; max/ declares none, so the empty rows have no result and drop out of the query and out of the write alike (A12).
-- Neither q's negative infinity nor Haskell's exception on maximum of the empty list is available here: the ruling is that an identityless fold over nothing produces nothing.
--! registry ../registries/143-row-fold-empty.reg
--! expect total = 8 0 15 0
--! expect peak = 5 -1 9 -1

--! out 8 0 15 0
+/ Readings@row

--! out 5 9
max/ Readings@row

--! out 3 2
min/ Readings@row

Bag , Total = +/ Readings@row
Bag , Peak = max/ Readings@row
